  description:
  - The Emerald Lumen Moths were one of the first newly documented species since
    the Mist entombed the region. The hairs on their upper adbomen secrete an enzyme
    that rapidly encourages growth on select plant protiens, acting as a catalyst
    to a plant's otherwise dormant growth.
  - This coupled with the fact that their hairs carry pollen with ease makes their
    symbiosis with the local flora almost essential for an ecosystem to thrive. A
    decrease in the local moth population could prove devastating to an ecosystem.
  leftText: 
  rightText: The Emerald Lumen Moths were one of the first newly documented species
    since the Mist entombed the region. The hairs on their upper adbomen secrete
    an enzyme that rapidly encourages growth on select plant protiens, acting as
    a catalyst to a plant's otherwise dormant growth. This coupled with the fact
    that their hairs carry pollen with ease makes their symbiosis with the local
    flora almost essential for an ecosystem to thrive. A decrease in the local moth
    population could prove devastating to an ecosystem.
